  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at White Eagle Hall in Jersey City, New Jersey, on Friday, November 10, 2017 [1][3]. This concert was part of their Goths tour, which also featured the band Mothers [3]. The event is documented by a poster credited to Greg Cristman [3]. The available recording, titled tMG2017-11-10, was taped by Bryce Carr and transferred by notasfarwest [1]. It captures a 114-minute set consisting of 23 songs [1]. The performance opened with “The Grey King and the Silver Flame Attunement” from the album Goths [1]. The setlist included tracks such as “Cotton” from We Shall All Be Healed and “In the Craters on the Moon” from Heretic Pride [1]. Listeners can hear the rare song “Beautiful Gas Mask” from All Eternals Deck, which has only eight archived performances [1][2]. The show featured a bustout of “Night Light” from Transcendental Youth, marking its first appearance in 68 archived shows [1][2]. Other songs included “Moon Over Goldsboro” from Get Lonely and the unreleased track “I’ve Got the Sex” [1]. The set continued with “Snow Crush Killing Song” from Sweden and “Paid in Cocaine” from Goths [1]. Additional songs from Goths, such as “Shelved” and “Broom People” from The Sunset Tree, were also played [1]. The performance concluded with a five-song encore, including “The Diaz Brothers” and “Up the Wolves” [1]. This recording is the only one available for this specific date in the archive [1].",
